{{!-- The two port scripts that are NOT loaded by a tag: reader-core.js
     injects read-tools.js, and ask-workspace.js imports ask-jobs.js.
     Both built their own URL as ...?v=__FR_VER, one constant for every
     file, while Ghost hashes each asset separately. So the URL for
     read-tools.js never changed when read-tools.js did, and with
     max-age=31536000 the CDN kept handing out the old object: a fix
     verified present on the server was still absent in the browser.
     Passing the real {{asset}} URLs through data attributes gives each
     file its own hash. A data attribute rather than a global because
     setting a global here would need inline script, which the CSP
     forbids. --}}
<div id="frPortAssets" hidden
     data-read-tools="{{asset "js/port/read-tools.js"}}&amp;frv=f236a19eeb0bd91a"
